{"name":"Chilli Oil","hex":"#9d453c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chilli","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of chili."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chilli"},{"term":"oil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Liquid fat.","Petroleum-based liquid used as fuel or lubricant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lubricate with oil.","To grease with oil for cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chili oil","blocks":[{"text":"Chili oil or chile oil is a condiment made from vegetable oil that has been infused with chili peppers. Different types of oil and hot peppers are used, and other components may also be included. It is commonly used in Chinese cuisine, Mexico, Italy, and elsewhere. It is particularly popular in Chinese cuisine, especially western Chinese cuisines, such as Sichuan cuisine, Hunan cuisine, Guizhou cuisine, and Shaanxi cuisine, where it is used as an ingredient in cooked dishes, as well as a condiment. It is sometimes used as a dip for meat and dim sum. It is also employed in the Korean Chinese noodle soup dish jjamppong. A closely related condiment in Chinese cuisine is chili crisp, which contains edible chunks of food and chilis in oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Chilioil.jpg/330px-Chilioil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chili_oil"},{"title":"Oil","blocks":[{"text":"Oil is a liquid with varying degrees of viscosity depending on temperature. Oil is any nonpolar chemical substance that is composed primarily of hydrocarbons and is hydrophobic and lipophilic. Oils are usually flammable and surface active. Most oils are unsaturated lipids that are liquid at room temperature."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Rayu.jpg/500px-Rayu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Rayu.jpg/1280px-Rayu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Rayu.jpg/500px-Rayu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Taberu rāyu on top of steamed rice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARayu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Manti_of_Kayseri.jpg/500px-Manti_of_Kayseri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Manti_of_Kayseri.jpg/1280px-Manti_of_Kayseri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Manti_of_Kayseri.jpg/500px-Manti_of_Kayseri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Turkish mantı with garlic yogurt and red pepper paste infused oil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManti_of_Kayseri.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Italian_olive_oil_2007.jpg/500px-Italian_olive_oil_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Italian_olive_oil_2007.jpg/500px-Italian_olive_oil_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bottle of olive oil used in food","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalian_olive_oil_2007.jpg"}],"sounds":{"chilli":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-chilli.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common